  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This paper proposes and tests, using ab initio metadynamics simulations, DFT adsorption tests, and early-age hydration experiments, that 3-aminopropyl triethoxysilane (APTES) adsorbed on Ca3SiO5 surfaces shields penta-coordinated surface calcium, changes dissolution from favorable toward non-spontaneous, lowers early Ca2+ concentrations in solution, and thereby retards the initial hydration of cement.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
